legend64
Copyright 2026 Jonathan Kimmitt

An RV64GC processor core, a system-on-chip around it for the Xilinx VC707 board, and the
software to run Debian on it. Designed and written with Claude (Anthropic).

Unless a file says otherwise, this work is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see LICENSE). Files carry an SPDX-License-Identifier line.

Parts under other terms
-----------------------

linux/drivers/legend_eth.c, linux/kernel/patches/
    The Ethernet driver for the Linux kernel and the patch that adds it: GPL-2.0, as a part of
    the kernel must be.

linux/dts/legend64-vc707.dts
    Dual licensed, GPL-2.0-only or MIT, as is usual for device trees.

Third-party material in this repository
---------------------------------------

sw/coremark/
    CoreMark, Copyright 2018 Embedded Microprocessor Benchmark Consortium (EEMBC).
    Apache License 2.0, together with EEMBC's CoreMark acceptable use terms
    (https://www.eembc.org/coremark/). core_portme.c and core_portme.h are this project's
    port of it.

sw/dhrystone/
    Dhrystone 2.1 by Reinhold P. Weicker (C version by Rick Richardson), as distributed with
    PicoRV32. The benchmark carries no licence statement; it has been freely redistributed
    since 1988. stdlib.c, the small C library beside it, is public domain (the Unlicense).

fpga/litedram/build/
    Output of LiteDRAM's standalone core generator for the configuration in
    fpga/litedram/vc707.yml: the DDR3 controller and PHY (litedram_core.v) and the register
    headers its initialisation software needs. LiteX and LiteDRAM are Copyright EnjoyDigital
    and contributors, BSD 2-Clause (https://github.com/enjoy-digital/litex,
    https://github.com/enjoy-digital/litedram).

fpga/third_party/verilog-ethernet/axis_gmii_tx.sv
    The transmit side of the byte-stream Ethernet MAC: Alex Forencich's verilog-ethernet
    (Copyright 2015-2018, MIT), as modified for lowRISC's ariane-ethernet to expose the frame
    check sequence, with one correction made here: that modification counted the inter-frame
    gap only once after reset, so every later frame followed one byte time behind the last.

fpga/litedram/vc707_ddr3_pins.xdc
    The VC707's DDR3 pin assignments and I/O standards, taken from the constraints Xilinx's
    Memory Interface Generator writes for this board.

Third-party material used when building
---------------------------------------

Submodules under third_party/ and ref/ (see README.md), each under its own licence. A bitstream
or boot image built from this repository contains or runs:

    eth_mac_1g, axis_gmii_rx, axis_gmii_tx, lfsr    Alex Forencich, verilog-ethernet, MIT
      (as carried in third_party/synthgui)
    LiteEth SGMII PHY (1000BASE-X PCS, GTX wrapper)  EnjoyDigital and contributors, BSD 2-Clause
      (generated; as carried in third_party/synthgui)
    liblitedram (DDR3 initialisation and levelling,  EnjoyDigital and contributors, BSD 2-Clause
      linked into the boot monitor; third_party/litex)
    OpenSBI (third_party/opensbi)                    Western Digital and contributors, BSD 2-Clause
    Linux kernel (downloaded by the build)           GPL-2.0
    BusyBox (initramfs; not included)                GPL-2.0

The ISA tests run by scripts/isa_legend64.sh are the upstream riscv-tests (ref/riscv-tests,
BSD 3-Clause); ref/picorv32 is ISC. scripts/lockstep_qemu.py compares the core with QEMU
(GPL-2.0), which is not included.
